    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\n9 Hammond Street is a most attractive red brick mid-terrace residence, originally constructed in the early 1900's and fully renovated and extended in 2014. Ideally positioned within this highly regarded and convenient Dublin 8 location, the property is presented in excellent condition throughout and successfully combines period charm with a contemporary specification and a warm, inviting interior.\nExtending to approximately 74 sq.m., the accommodation is thoughtfully laid out and provides bright, well-balanced living space ideally suited to modern day requirements.\nAt ground floor level, an entrance porch and welcoming living room lie to the front of the property. This is a particularly comfortable space, enhanced by timber flooring and a feature solid fuel stove, creating an appealing focal point. To the rear, the kitchen/dining room is fitted with modern cabinetry and offers a bright, open-plan layout with direct access to the rear garden.\nUpstairs, there are two well-proportioned bedrooms together with a stylishly appointed bathroom, finished to a high standard and featuring contemporary fittings.\nThis sought-after area is home to some of Dublin's finest cafés and restaurants, including Marlowe & Co, Gaillot et Gray, Fumbally, Hens Teeth, Bastible and Two Pups Coffee. The property is also within easy reach of a number of respected schools and educational institutions such as Griffith College Dublin, Canal Way Educate Together, Griffith Barracks Multi-Denominational School, St. Catherine's National School, Loreto College St. Stephen's Green, and Trinity College Dublin.\nA wide range of amenities are located nearby, including Iveagh Gardens, St. Stephen's Green, the Phoenix Park, St. James' Hospital, the new National Children's Hospital, and Heuston Station.\nThe property is also exceptionally well served by public transport, with both the Red and Green LUAS lines within walking distance, a number of regular bus routes servicing the area, and Dublin Bikes stations nearby, making a car a luxury rather than a necessity."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nPorch - \nTimber floor, door to living room.\n\nLiving Room - \nTimber floor, solid fuel stove, storage, window to the front, under stairs storage cupboard.\n\nKitchen - \nTimber floor, double glazed doors to rear garden, window with privacy glass, stainless steel counter, electric oven and gas hob, wall and floor units.\n\nLanding - \nVelux window, recessed lighting.\n\nBedroom 1 - \nDouble bedroom, window to rear, built in wardrobe, recessed lighting, shelving.\n\nBedroom 2 - \nDouble bedroom, window to front, attic access.\n\nBathroom - \nTiled floor, partially tiled walls, heated towel rail, free standing bath with clawed feet, WC, wash hand basin, Velux, shelving.\n\n"
      },
